.i la jongausib cu cusku di'e
> brailyle'u is not a valid lujvo. You can't have a fu'ivla and a gismu as
> a veljvo.

Yes, you can. The PEG morphology gives every fu'ivla at least one rafsi.=20
You can add 'y or remove the last vowel and replace it with y. The first=20
method always works, but the second one works too in this case. (That=20
means we could equally well say "braile'yle'u" instead")

> braile: "x1 is a braille letter/symbol in braille alphabet/character-set
> x2 representing x3" (I know it's almost the same as the one Pierre
> suggested)

It's very different. Pierre suggested "x1 is written in braile" not "x1=20
is a letter of the braile alphabet". If braile is taken to mean the=20
former, then a lujvo like brailyle'u will be needed to refer to the=20
actual letters of the braile alphabet.

